From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:53:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-93: snaplines on the text baselines, like WPF
 (0.93.0)

WPF (Create UIs > Snaplines): "alignment boundaries appear when the edges and
the text of some controls are aligned". Here only the edges and centres
snapped. Now snapLines() also collects the neighbours' text baselines
(baselineOf: a label's / button's own text via a Range and the font's
ascent / descent, a panel's caption, a text box's value in the middle of its
content box; at most 400) and the dragged one's own baseline offset; a move
snaps its baseline onto one when that is nearer than an edge line, and the
guide is drawn dashed. Alt still means no snapping.

WPF_DIFF_LOG.md: item 22 done (0.92 commit filled in); the Blend pages added
as sources (artboard modifier keys, keyboard shortcuts) with new open items
23-27, and two recorded as not changed (Alt+drag copies / Ctrl+wheel pans in
Blend -- this designer follows VS: Ctrl+drag copies, Alt = no snapping,
Ctrl+wheel zooms).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 183, panels, real VS Code 157):
probe (a 12 px text put 2 px below a 40 px text's baseline, dragged sideways:
its baseline lands on it, off by 0.00, the guide dashed; both pages).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
